# Copy this file to `keystore.properties` (sibling, gitignored) and fill
# in the release signing values when you cut your first release build.
#
# Debug builds (`gradlew assembleDebug` / `installDebug`) do NOT need any
# of these — Gradle uses the default Android debug keystore.
#
# Release builds (`gradlew assembleRelease`) do. Without these values
# the release task fails with "Cannot recover key" or similar.
#
# Generating a keystore (one-time):
#   keytool -genkey -v -keystore sailline-release.keystore `
#     -alias sailline -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000
#
# Move sailline-release.keystore to a safe place OUTSIDE this repo
# (it's gitignored by *.keystore, but better not to even drop it here).
#
# Then point at it from `keystore.properties`:

storeFile=C:\\Users\\grayv\\Secrets\\sailline-release.keystore
storePassword=CHANGE_ME
keyAlias=sailline
keyPassword=CHANGE_ME

# Transistorsoft licence — ALSO read by the Gradle build for the SDK
# entitlement. It's already set in ~/.gradle/gradle.properties for normal
# dev. If you need a per-repo override (e.g., shipping a build for a
# different bundle id under a different licence), set it here and it
# wins over the user-global properties.
#
# TRANSISTOR_LICENSE=...
